# Corevia detached application preview

This experimental application keeps your code in `app/`, `routes/`, `resources/`
and `config/`. Framework dependencies live in `vendor/corevia-framework/runtime`.
The runtime package is a local V4 prototype, not a published registry release.

Install dependencies using the sibling `runtime/` directory from this preview:

```sh
composer install --no-interaction --no-scripts --no-plugins
php corevia serve
```

Run the included application smoke check with `php corevia test`.

Open http://127.0.0.1:8081. No database is required. Optionally install one auth kit:

```sh
php corevia starter:auth --stack=bootstrap
# Alternatives: --stack=tailwind or --stack=react
```

Serve only `public/`. Build dependencies off-server before uploading to a host
without Composer. This first preview does not yet supply a shared-host upload
layout, cloud adapters, a package registry release or a V3-to-V4 upgrade tool.
Never expose the project root, vendor/, storage/ or configuration as public files.
No optional AI/provider credentials are enabled automatically.
